body:
After some experiments and looking at the code, I think I found the issue: it's the _notification() behavior of rich_text_label.cpp:

		case NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE: {
			_stop_thread();
	--->		if (!text.is_empty()) {
	--->			set_text(text);
			}

			main->first_invalid_line.store(0); // Invalidate all lines.
			queue_redraw();
		} break;

I did some testing. When the RLT is added to a tree, if the text isn't empty, it looks like it calls set_text, replacing the stack with the text property. Calling add_text() to an empty RTL before adding it to the tree works as expected (this confused me a lot, since it works some of the time, before I decided to dig deep into this. And it's probably why this behavior manages to stay hidden).

I don't know why it's necessary to call set_text() on tree enter, nor how to fix this. I really don't know how Godot works.

If you can confirm my findings, I would change the title of the issue to something like: "RichTextLabel: if the text property isn't empty, it calls set_text() on tree entering, silently clearing the stack."
